## Shared cultural events (possible distraction windows)

| Dates | Event | Scale |
|---|---|---|
| 2026-11-26 | Thanksgiving 2026 | 3 |

Weeks inside a scale-3 shared event have run quieter than average (lower headline, falling attention), but the first week after one closes has carried a higher-than-usual rate of major corporate episodes: announcements held through the event tend to land as soon as it ends. Plan releases for the window itself or well after it, not the week it closes.

Historical changes are averages of week-over-week moves in the headline (percentile points) during weeks containing that kind of catalyst, 2015 onward, against all other weeks. They describe tendency, not prediction.

